            "review_title": "Review at Banh Xeo Chao 85",
            "review_text": "V00Doo\nKuala Lumpur, Malaysia529 contributions\n0\nHCMC speciality in Nha Trang\nJan 2020\nThis was our 2nd choice as the other restaurant was closed for Tet holidays. The seating is split over 3 floors, with narrow, steep stairs with little headroom. Not quite the cleanest, but none of us got sick throughout the trip. \nWe ordered 2 types of bánh xèo (bahn SAY-oh) - shrimp & pork and 2 orders of spring rolls. The spring rolls arrived pretty quickly and they were sizzling hot! But sooooo good!!\nUnfortunately, the bánh xèo was not up to expectations (compared to the bánh xèo street in HCMC - crisp edges but less tasty and very oily! Unlimited vegetables/herbs, pickled carrot/radish and sweet chili-vinegar sauce but no complimentary vietnamese tea. If you come in a big group, be prepared to split up. Cash ONLY.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten January 28, 2020",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-11",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
